<title>UK: UNITED NEWS TO BUY 15 PCT BLENHEIM STAKE - FT.</title>
<headline>UNITED NEWS TO BUY 15 PCT BLENHEIM STAKE - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French water utility Compagnie Generale des Eaux has agreed to sell its 15 percent stake in British exhibitions company Blenheim Group Plc to United News &amp; Media , the Financial Times reported.</p>
<p>United has reportedly been considering a 520p per share bid for Blenheim, which would value the company at about 480 million stg.</p>
<p>Dutch publisher VNU , which bought what it described as a strategic long-term 15 percent stake in Blenheim last week, is expected to buy a further 10 percent, the FT said, possibly as early as Tuesday.</p>
<p>VNU said it reserved the right to bid for Blenheim if a third party were to do the same.</p>
<p>The FT said United was still consulting with its advisers about whether to launch a bid.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
